# Auth & identity (Chaupaal)

## Model (Instagram-style)

- **One Firebase Auth identity** per email **or** phone signup (password and/or Google).
- **Many Chaupaal profiles** under that identity — **no hard profile-create cap** (Instagram: unlimited owned; their “5” is simultaneous device logins of separate credentials, not our profile model).
- App uses **active profile** (`activeProfileId`) for posts, chats, display name, username.
- Account switcher lists all profiles under the signed-in identity.

## Signup / contact

- Signup requires **verified email (Gmail/Google or email+password)** **or** **verified phone** (OTP).
- When a user adds email or phone at any stage, **verify with OTP / Firebase verification before treating it as registered**.
- Phone is for signup and recovery/linking; OTP required when phone is used.
- Unverified email/password users **stay signed in** after login; show a persistent, dismissible-but-recurring **verify-email banner** (resend CTA). Do **not** sign them out / kick back to login. Keep `hasVerifiedContact` as the gate for flows that truly require verification.

## Login (unified identifier)

- Password login accepts **username, email, or phone** in one field (`loginIdentifier`).
- Email → `signInWithEmailAndPassword` directly.
- Username / phone → pre-auth `POST /api/media-config` `{ action: 'resolve_identifier' }` → `{ email }` or generic `{ notFound: true }` (no enumeration details).
- Same generic error for not-found and wrong password: “Incorrect username/email/phone or password”.
- `phoneIndex/{e164}` stores `{ uid, email }` when a phone is verified/linked so phone can resolve to an email for password login.

## Phone + password

- After phone OTP (signup or later), prefer **linking** `EmailAuthProvider.credential(email, password)` onto the Firebase user so the account is password-resolvable.
- If no email is available, skip linking and surface a profile note: add email to enable password login with phone.
- Existing phone-only accounts (no `password` provider): on next successful phone-OTP login, show a **skippable interstitial** to set email+password (`linkWithCredential`); re-prompt next login if still missing (same dismiss/reappear idea as the verify-email banner — not a separate reminder system).

## Username

- Globally unique handle; **one profile per username**.
- Rename allowed; **old username freed immediately** (Rename A).

## Profile type (signup)

- Default **Personal**. UI is a small Personal / Professional **toggle**, not a forked flow.
- Professional optionally collects **Industry** and **Purpose** (top-N from `industryStats` / `purposeStats` + “Other — type your own”). Both optional; counters increment on register (`FieldValue.increment`).
- Gender remains **mandatory for Personal** (optional for Professional). Include **Prefer to self-describe** + required free-text when selected.

## Session persistence

- Stay signed in on the device across app restarts (**Firebase Auth local persistence**).
- Clear session **only** on explicit logout (or remote session revoke).
- Soft reset for pre-launch: re-register OK; do not build legacy migration this pass.

## Passwords

- Email + password + Google + forgot-password (email reset; resolve identifier → email when needed).
- Do not invent separate payment/auth stacks per feature.
